good morning so we just woke up and  we're gonna get ready for the day yeah  yeah I'm Sarah and I try to live  zero-waste with a baby being zero-waste  to me means not using single-use  plastics getting my food in my own  reusable containers or from the farmers  market package free and also composting  all of my food waste I started on mine  zero waste journey about five years ago  I also started a blog to chronicle all  my experiences to help other people on  their journey as well and I opened a  zero waste lifestyle shop a really  common image of zero wasters today are  you'll see like them carrying some trash  in a mason jar which is definitely  really admirable but I feel like can be  very intimidating as well and I  definitely make more trash than what  fits in a jar  sometimes my baby just wants to be  attached to me all day and I don't have  time or energy to make my own food so  sometimes I'll have someone deliver food  but the effort behind reducing my waste  I think is just as important in terms of  a baby a means using reusables instead  of disposable as like diapers and wipes  I'm really lucky that I can work part  time from home and I can breastfeed her  like on demand right now it's pretty  easy since she's only 3 months old that  she is just breastfed but I am already  looking into when she starts eating  solids and planning for snacks and  things like that and hopefully I can not  use disposables there as well we didn't  start out cloth diapering right when we  got home from the hospital I was  actually really intimidated at first  because nobody taught me how to use  cloth diapers I kind of just used  youtube videos and tutorials online to  figure it out but once we got into the  habit of it I really enjoyed it  because you're not constantly running  out and running out of diapers and  having to take out the trash all the  time we're having a trash can full of  stinky diapers instead I just do the  laundry it's really easy it's not a more  complicated way of do  laundry it's just like doing another  load of laundry here's my diaper caddy I  like to use pre folds and then here's  the inserts and some cloth wipes you  just fold this around the baby and then  you can use this thing here that has  plastic clasps on it and that will  secure the pre fold diaper on to her and  then to finish it off you just put a  wool cover on top and they also double  those pants wool naturally is  antibacterial and it wicks away any  moisture so you don't feel any dampness  on the outside and then the soiled  diaper I just throw into a wet bag right  here and that's it washing cloth diapers  is really easy I just rinsed them off  you can rinse them with a bidet attached  to your toilet and then once you are  ready to do a load you just put them in  the washing machine you don't have to  use any fancy detergent they probably do  laundry for heard diapers every other  day anytime we've used like a disposable  wipe you end up having to use so many  even though I just use these like  flannel pieces of fabric and then I just  let them with water you end up saving so  much money I mean like you can go  through a pack of wipes like really  quickly any time I've put like a  disposable on her and she goes number  two it always ends up in a blowout and  it like goes up I've tried different  brands different sizes and it's just I  don't know I've never had that issue  with cloth diapers though they seem to  absorb a lot more a typical day for us  is we wake up in the morning and I feed  her sometimes I will pump in the morning  and then give that a bottle to my  husband to feed her and then we play a  little bit  and change her diaper and kind of just  repeat that all day it's nap time she  fell asleep on top of me so I'll just be  hanging out so she's got a clean diaper  a clean clothes she's already taking her  first nap so now I have her in her  carrier and we can do some errands  around the house some chores now I'm  gonna do a load of laundry and it's all  just in this wet bag here you think I'd  just dump it all that making some tea  and some oats just in case I don't have  a chance to make anything really so I  did a load of laundry and I made some  food to eat I have made some tea for  myself and she ended up falling asleep  in the carrier so I'm going to do some  work on the computer okay  now we're at the farmers market and  we're just gonna get some vegetables for  the week just finished up with the  market and I put everything in my  reusable bag and my shopping cart and I  was also able to get a drink too today I  have a kale salad and I'm also has some  cabbage and some roasted sweet potato  that I got from the farmers market and  then I made  lemon tahini dressing and I'm just going  to top it off with some hemp parts that  I bought in a large bag but not from in  like a bulk section just because it's  harder for me to get to the grocery  store and fill all my bags of course the  hardest part is finding a time to eat it  because she's not happy right now okay  so I just put her to bed and now I have  some free time to do whatever I want  being zero waste the way that we are  today is not some sort of new concept  reusing and saving and buying secondhand  like these are things that our  grandparents have been doing for  generations I think about how I grew up  and how I was so fortunate to be able to  go camping and see all these great  national parks and experience nature and  it worries me that she might not get to  experience those same things and I want  to make sure that I'm doing things to  preserve the world around us the way  that I side  [Music]
 

